<div class="page">
  <div class="sl">Likutay Halachos &middot; Yoreh De&apos;ah, Part Two</div>
  <div class="mt">Laws of Chalah</div>
  <div class="st">Hilchos Chalah</div>
  <div class="dv">&middot; &middot; &#10022; &middot; &middot;</div>
  <div class="ht">Halacha Four</div>
  <div class="pt">Part One &mdash; Sections &#x05D0;&ndash;&#x05D5;</div>
  <div class="cr">Based on the Torah <em>&ldquo;Yisrael na&rsquo;asim adonim l&rsquo;ba&rsquo;alayhem&rdquo;</em> [Israel become masters over their masters] &mdash; Likutay [Moharan] II, Section 76. See there.</div>

  <div class="pream">The matter of <em>Chalah</em><sup>*</sup> which differs from <em>Terumos</em> and <em>Ma&rsquo;asros</em> in that it is practiced even in this time outside the Land of Israel, even though we are all ritually impure from contact with the dead &mdash; so that the Torah of <em>Chalah</em> should not be forgotten from Israel.</div>
  <div style="font-family:'EB Garamond',Georgia,serif;font-size:14px;color:#6b3a1f;border-left:3px solid #c4a45a;padding:8px 14px;margin-bottom:20px;background:#ede0c0;border-radius:2px;"><sup>*</sup> <em>Chalah</em> (lit. the portion of dough separated and given to the Kohen) &mdash; for the full exposition of its deeper meaning as understood throughout these halachos, the reader is referred to the opening of Halacha 1 of Hilchos Chalah above.</div>

  <div class="sm first">Section One &middot; &#x05D0;</div>
  <p class="ni">The general principle: in every place where Israel comes in exile, at first they are there subdued in exile, and they have great sufferings in physical and spiritual matters, each one according to his level etc. &mdash; for they wander and roam and are buffeted there and are despised there in the eyes of the vast majority etc. etc. But afterward they conquer that very place itself and raise and elevate that place together with all that is within it, so that it be blessed &mdash; in the aspect of <em>&ldquo;v&rsquo;nish&rsquo;ar gam hu le&rsquo;Elokaynu&rdquo;</em> [and he shall remain also to our G-d] &mdash; the initial letters of which spell <em>golah</em> [exile]. In the aspect of the future: the theatres and circuses (<em>batay tartiyas</em>) etc. will become places where Torah is taught publicly &mdash; as it is said: <em>&ldquo;and he shall remain also to our G-d&rdquo;</em> (Zecharyah 9:7) &mdash; as our Sages of blessed memory said etc. See there.</p>

  <div class="sm">Section Two &middot; &#x05D1;</div>
  <p class="ni">And this is the aspect of <em>Chalah</em> and all priestly gifts (<em>matenos kehunah</em>) given specifically from food items, and principally from the produce of the Land: which are <em>Terumah</em>, <em>Bikkurim</em>, <em>Ma&rsquo;asros</em>, and <em>Chalah</em> which comes last etc. For the reason Israel is subdued in exile at first in every place they are driven &mdash; this is because in every place there are very many holy sparks (<em>nitzotzos</em>) and holy souls that were thrust away, scattered, and dispersed there through the sin of the first Adam and through the sins of all generations until this very day. And these sparks and souls are always waiting and hoping that an Israelite man will come there. And as soon as an Israelite man comes there, they fall upon him, surround him, and cling to him, in order that he rectify them. And because these sparks are lodged among the nations and among the <em>klippos</em> [husks], which grip them and press them tightly &mdash; on account of this the Israelite man who comes there has great sufferings. For the <em>klippos</em> etc. and all the evil and alien thoughts and confusions etc. that come from them cling to him &mdash; because they see that the sparks want to be rectified. And the essential time of their clinging and provocations is when this man engages in some holy matter, for that is the time of rectification and redemption of the sparks from among the nations and <em>klippos</em> &mdash; as is known. All of this is understood in the writings of our master of blessed memory (<em>Rabbaynu z&rdquo;l</em>) in many places, and is alluded to in the writings of the Zohar and all the writings of the holy Ari of blessed memory, which are among the great foundations upon which the Ari&rsquo;s writings and the Zohar are built &mdash; as is known to the understanding, in countless places.</p>
  <p>And this is the aspect of <em>&ldquo;let the burden of work be heavy upon the men&rdquo;</em> etc. (<em>tichbad ha&rsquo;avodah</em>) (Shemos 5:9), the aspect of <em>&ldquo;and since I came to Pharaoh to speak in Your name, he has made things worse for this people&rdquo;</em> etc. (Shemos 5:23). And this is the great force of the length of the exile, particularly now &mdash; for the closer one gets to the end (<em>ketz</em>), the more all the opponents of holiness, and the <em>klippos</em>, desires, trials, and confusions etc., grow stronger and more provocative &mdash; as is explained elsewhere. And one needs very, very great strengthening against them, and to hope and wait for the salvation of Hashem at every moment and in every place where one comes in exile and wandering &mdash; until Hashem looks down and sees from Heaven. And then one will merit not only to go out and rise from there to freedom oneself, but also to clarify and raise from there very many sparks belonging to the portion of the root of one&rsquo;s soul &mdash; in the aspect of <em>&ldquo;and he shall remain also to our G-d&rdquo;</em> &mdash; until even that place itself becomes sanctified in great holiness, where Torah will be taught publicly, in the aspect of the theatres and circuses etc. And this is the aspect of <em>&ldquo;and afterward they shall go out with great wealth&rdquo;</em> (<em>v&rsquo;acharay chain yaitzay&rsquo;u birechush gadol</em>) (Beraishis 15:14) &mdash; which was also said concerning this exile as is known. As our Sages of blessed memory said: <em>&ldquo;and also that nation&rdquo;</em> &mdash; to include the exile of all four kingdoms.</p>

  <div class="sm">Section Three &middot; &#x05D2;</div>
  <p class="ni">And this is the aspect of <em>Chalah</em> etc. For the essential holy sparks fell in particular into matters of food &mdash; because the beginning of their fall was through the sin of the first Adam who sinned through eating: the eating of the Tree of Knowledge of good and evil. And therefore great labors are required before the food is clarified from its dross (<em>psoles</em>), both physically and spiritually. And this is especially so in what grows from the earth, and in particular in wheat and the five grain species which are called <em>lechem</em> [bread] and are the essential satisfying food &mdash; as our Sages of blessed memory said. And therefore there are many labors in [producing] bread before it is clarified from its dross: plowing and sowing etc., reaping, threshing, winnowing, separating, grinding, sifting, kneading, and baking &mdash; before one tastes the taste of bread. And likewise there are several commandments in bread, which are ten commandments as our Sages of blessed memory said &mdash; in order to clarify the wheat and flour and bread etc. from chaff and straw etc. spiritually. For the essential rectification is through the holiness of the commandments that apply to them, and the essential clarification is through faith (<em>emunah</em>) as is known.</p>
  <p>And one must be strong in faith until one merits the illumination of the Will (<em>he&rsquo;arat haratzon</em>) at the time of eating &mdash; that one will yearn and long for Hashem blessed-be-He with an extraordinary will (<em>ratzon muflag</em>) etc. &mdash; as is explained in the Torah <em>&ldquo;Ki merachamam yenagaim&rdquo;</em> [for He who has compassion upon them will lead them] etc. (Likutay [Moharan] II, Section 7). See there. And as I heard and understood then from his holy conversation which he spoke at that time, which was printed alongside the stories. See there. That a person must strengthen himself only in perfect faith without any investigations (<em>chakirot</em>), and then through faith one merits to ascend to Will, to the point that one will yearn and long for Hashem blessed-be-He with an extraordinary will beyond measure etc.</p>
  <p>And the illumination of the Will is merited at the time of eating specifically, through the encompassing of the worlds, through the illumination of <em>ben v&rsquo;talmid</em> [son and disciple] etc. &mdash; those who make known to them the true knowledge that Hashem is G-d (<em>ki Hashem hu ha&rsquo;Elokim</em>), from which comes the essential holy faith. And therefore one must give the firstfruits (<em>raishis</em>) to the Kohen from the foodstuffs &mdash; for the Kohen is the aspect of the totality of <em>ben v&rsquo;talmid</em> as explained in the aforementioned Torah. For through giving the gifts to the Kohen who is composed of <em>ben v&rsquo;talmid</em> &mdash; through this faith is completed and clarifies all the clarifications, and raises them to the Will, until one merits the illumination of the Will at the time of eating specifically. For the essential eating and satisfaction is from the Will &mdash; in the aspect of <em>&ldquo;and He satisfies every living thing with will&rdquo;</em> (<em>u&rsquo;masbi&rsquo;a l&rsquo;chol chai ratzon</em>) (Tehillim 145:16). And as it is written: <em>&ldquo;Naftali is sated with will and full of the blessing of Hashem&rdquo;</em> (<em>Naftali sva ratzon u&rsquo;malay birkas Hashem</em>) (Devarim 33:23) &mdash; which was said in praise of the fruits of his land. And likewise <em>&ldquo;and he was the favorite of his brothers and dipped his foot in oil&rdquo;</em> etc. (ibid. v.24) &mdash; as Rashi explained there.</p>
  <p>And the essential flavor and delight of food is drawn from the supernal Will (<em>ratzon ha&rsquo;elyon</em>). And every person must strengthen himself at the time of eating to raise everything to its root &mdash; that he merit through eating the illumination of the Will as mentioned, which is the essential wholeness of the clarification and elevation of all the sparks in the food when they ascend to the supernal Will, which is their supernal root &mdash; as is known. And every person can merit this through the power of the true tzaddik in whom shines the illumination of <em>ben v&rsquo;talmid</em> as mentioned. Through which one merits at the time of eating the illumination of the Will as mentioned. For the essential rectification and clarification of the sparks is through the illumination of <em>ben v&rsquo;talmid</em> as mentioned &mdash; that is: through illuminating in all the low and fallen places &mdash; for Hashem is still with them etc., in the aspect of <em>&ldquo;the whole earth is full of His glory&rdquo;</em> (<em>melo chol ha&rsquo;aretz kevodo</em>), in the aspect of <em>&ldquo;awaken and sing, you who dwell in the dust&rdquo;</em> (<em>hakitzu v&rsquo;ranenu shochnay afar</em>) (Yeshayahu 26:19) etc. For the sparks that fell to where they fell are in the aspect of <em>shochnay afar</em> [dwellers in the dust], for they are placed on the very lowest level. And the essential clarification and elevation is through this aspect of illuminating the lowest dwellers, the aspect of <em>&ldquo;awaken and sing, you who dwell in the dust&rdquo;</em> etc. as mentioned. And therefore through this one merits the illumination of the Will at the time of eating etc.</p>
  <p>And every person must strengthen himself to go with the aforementioned Torah, to constantly strengthen himself in Hashem blessed-be-He and to never despair of himself under any circumstances &mdash; only to always know that the whole earth is full of His glory, and Hashem is still with him and near him etc. &mdash; until he merits to strengthen himself at the time of eating, that the illumination of the Will reaches him specifically at the time of eating: a strong and intense longing (<em>hishtokekus</em>) for Hashem blessed-be-He with very great will etc. as is explained there.</p>
  <p>And this is precisely the opposite of the falls of most of the world, who generally fall in their minds (<em>noflin b&rsquo;da&rsquo;atayhem</em>) on account of their improper deeds, and many despair of themselves &mdash; as is known, this terrible illness under the sun. And most of the falls come through eating, as is explained in the words of our master of blessed memory in another place. Certainly as long as one does not merit holiness as is appropriate, one certainly does not eat in holiness and purity as is appropriate. And on account of this people often fall in their minds again and again because of eating &mdash; and in truth all of this is the work of the <em>ba&rsquo;al davar</em> [adversary]. For one is forbidden to fall in one&rsquo;s mind over anything, as is explained in our words countless times. On the contrary: one must strengthen oneself every time, every day, as mentioned &mdash; and in particular at the time of eating, when it is forbidden to be a lazy man (which they call <em>shleimazlnik</em>) as is explained there. Rather one must be a man of valor (<em>ish chayil</em>) until one merits the illumination of the Will at the time of eating specifically.</p>
  <p>That is: not only is it forbidden to fall in one&rsquo;s mind because of eating &mdash; on the contrary: one must know and believe that the eating of an Israelite man is very precious. For his eating is according to the Torah in any case &mdash; as he does not eat anything forbidden, heaven forbid, but everything according to the Torah &mdash; as it is written: <em>&ldquo;Your Torah is within my inward parts&rdquo;</em> (<em>v&rsquo;sorasecha b&rsquo;soch me&rsquo;ai</em>) (Tehillim 40:9) &mdash; as Rashi explained there: <em>&ldquo;all my eating is according to Your word.&rdquo;</em> And also he recites a blessing over every item before and after. And through this every Israelite man makes many clarifications through his eating &mdash; and he should eat with joy and with great strengthening in Hashem blessed-be-He, and know that the whole earth is full of His glory and Hashem is with him etc. as mentioned &mdash; until he merits at the very time of eating the illumination of the Will, that he specifically then longs for Hashem blessed-be-He with very great will. And then it is the ultimate wholeness of the clarification of all the sparks that ascend to their supernal root as mentioned.</p>
  <p>And therefore: the closer food is to its completion &mdash; that is, when people enjoy it and feel its flavor &mdash; the more clarification it requires. And therefore at the time of completion of the grain and the fruits, one must separate from them <em>Bikkurim</em>, <em>Terumos</em>, and <em>Ma&rsquo;asros</em>. And afterward, when one makes flour from the grain and kneads it with water to make dough &mdash; which is when the essential completion of the grain occurs, that it becomes bread which is the essential food of man &mdash; then is the time of the essential clarification, because it is closest to completion. And then one must separate <em>Chalah</em> for the Kohen. For at the time of completion of the bread &mdash; when its flavor and satisfaction, drawn from the supernal Will, is felt in it &mdash; then is the essential rectification and clarification through the commandment of <em>Chalah</em> given to the Kohen who is composed of the illumination of <em>ben v&rsquo;talmid</em>. So that we merit at the time of eating bread the illumination of the Will &mdash; from which comes the essential flavor and satisfaction &mdash; which is the essential elevation and clarification of all the sparks when they ascend to the supernal Will, namely: when a person through them longs for Hashem blessed-be-He with extraordinary will etc. as mentioned.</p>

  <div class="sm">Section Four &middot; &#x05D3;</div>
  <p class="ni">And this is the essential sustenance of our life in the grip of this long, bitter exile &mdash; for we have nothing to sustain ourselves, and everything we want to do, whether Torah or prayer etc., they do not let us do in wholeness on account of the overwhelming force of the exile of soul and body that overpowers each and every person, as each one knows in himself. And the essential vitality of our lives is through the Will &mdash; through the perfect tzaddikim who shine the aforementioned illumination of <em>ben v&rsquo;talmid</em> in us, through which every person can merit the illumination of the Will at the time of eating, namely: to long for Hashem blessed-be-He with strong will etc. as mentioned. And through this we have hope to go out from exile in physical and spiritual matters &mdash; for the essential thing is the Will, as is brought in our words in many places.</p>
  <p>And as the <em>Kneses Yisrael</em> [Community of Israel] says to the nations and to the <em>sitrin achrinin</em> [other sides] that grow strong against them at every moment to prevent them with every manner of prevention, heaven forbid &mdash; Israel says to them: <em>&ldquo;why do you rouse and why do you stir up love until it pleases?&rdquo;</em> (<em>mah ta&rsquo;iru umah te&rsquo;oreru es ha&rsquo;ahavah ad shetechpatz</em>) (Shir HaShirim 2:7) &mdash; that is: what do you want to damage, heaven forbid, our love with Hashem blessed-be-He, since we still desire and long for Hashem blessed-be-He with strong and extraordinary will etc. And as is explained from this in another place (in Hilchos Erev, Halacha 3). See there.</p>

  <div class="sm">Section Five &middot; &#x05D4;</div>
  <p class="ni">And therefore the commandment of <em>Chalah</em> is practiced even in this time, even outside the Land of Israel &mdash; so that the Torah of <em>Chalah</em> not be forgotten from Israel. Which is not the case with <em>Terumos</em> and <em>Ma&rsquo;asros</em> which are not practiced outside the Land of Israel at all. For <em>Chalah</em> &mdash; because it comes at the end of the completion of the bread, when then is the essential revelation of the Will that illuminates at the time of eating as mentioned, which is the essential rectification of all the sparks, which is the essential rectification of the exile as mentioned &mdash; therefore it is practiced even now outside the Land of Israel, so that the Torah of <em>Chalah</em> not be forgotten from Israel. So that we merit even now with the commandment of <em>Chalah</em> &mdash; that is: even though we are so subdued in exile, nonetheless we must strengthen ourselves in faith in Hashem blessed-be-He, and know that Hashem blessed-be-He is still with us and beside us etc., and the Will is still free (<em>haratzon chofshi</em>). And we can strengthen ourselves until we merit the illumination of the Will, through which we clarify all the clarifications and the redemption comes in general and in particular, and it will be fulfilled: <em>&ldquo;and he shall remain also to our G-d&rdquo;</em> &mdash; as mentioned. All of which is merited through the commandment of <em>Chalah</em> by separating the firstfruits (<em>raishis</em>) for the Kohen who is composed of <em>ben v&rsquo;talmid</em>, through which one merits the illumination of the Will etc. as mentioned.</p>

  <div class="sm">Section Six &middot; &#x05D5;</div>
  <p class="ni">And therefore the measure (<em>shi&rsquo;ur</em>) of the commandment of <em>Chalah</em> is forty-three eggs (<em>mem-gimel baitzim</em>) &mdash; which is the aspect of <em>gam</em> [also] &mdash; the aspect of <em>&ldquo;v&rsquo;af gam zos bihyosam b&rsquo;eretz oyevayhem lo me&rsquo;astim&rdquo;</em> [and even this: when they are in the land of their enemies, I did not despise them] etc. (Vayikra 26:44). That is: even though Israel are in the land of their enemies, in places very far from holiness, and they are subdued there in exile in very great exile &mdash; nonetheless: <em>&ldquo;I did not despise them and I did not abhor them to destroy them, heaven forbid, for I am Hashem their G-d.&rdquo;</em> For I reveal to them that Hashem is still with them etc. And through this they raise all the distant places to holiness, in the aspect of <em>&ldquo;and he shall remain also to our G-d.&rdquo;</em> And this is the aspect of <em>Chalah</em> whose measure is forty-three eggs &mdash; the aspect of <em>gam</em> mentioned &mdash; the aspects of <em>&ldquo;v&rsquo;af gam zos&rdquo;</em> etc., the aspects of <em>&ldquo;v&rsquo;nish&rsquo;ar gam hu le&rsquo;Elokaynu&rdquo;</em> as mentioned.</p>

